<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  com.nuzantara.wa-bot-throughput-sentinel — the organ that watches whether the
  WhatsApp bot actually SERVES anyone (2026-08-23).

  Why it exists: on 2026-08-23 the bot was measured to have produced its last
  successful answer, and received its last inbound message-webhook, both at
  2026-07-30 01:23:58Z — 24 days of total silence — while /health returned 200,
  the broker gauge advanced every 30s, the breaker read closed with zero
  failures, the codex seat probe said ok, and the autoreply flag was true.
  Every one of those measures a COMPONENT. None measured THROUGHPUT. A queue
  depth of zero and a queue depth of zero-because-nothing-arrives are the same
  number, and nothing in the fleet watched the difference.

  Every 900s (15min) tick: scripts/wa_bot_throughput_sentinel.py reads
  max(received_at) off inbound_webhooks WHERE channel='whatsapp' and
  max(created_at) off wa_outbox WHERE status='done' (SELECT-only, PRODUCTION
  Postgres via the 127.0.0.1:15432 tunnel), and separates three conditions:
    bot_broken    p0      inbound fresh, outbound stale — messages arriving,
                          none answered. The loudest, and the one that would
                          have caught the real outage: replayed against it,
                          it fires at +1.5h.
    dead_channel  p0      both silent >48h, RAW age, evaluated 24/7 — this one
                          deliberately ignores business hours, because 24 days
                          of silence must never be excused by "it is Sunday".
    inbound_stale digest  nobody writing; business hours only.

  Business-hours discipline (Mon-Sat 08:00-20:00 Asia/Makassar) is inherited
  from com.nuzantara.wa-mirror-freshness-liveness, including its hard-won
  `max(newest, today_open)` floor, so a quiet overnight line is Law 6 and not a
  page. Exhaustively scanned over a 10-day replay, the longest silent window
  that floor can produce is 13.0h — bounded, self-correcting, well under the
  48h dead_channel threshold.

  PRO-ONLY, and for a reason distinct from its sibling's (superscar #10): this
  organ needs the PRODUCTION tunnel, and the tunnel is launchd-supervised HERE
  (com.balizero.wr2.pg-proxy, KeepAlive). On Mini the equivalent flyctl proxy
  is a bare unsupervised process — measured 2026-08-23: PID 8883, PPID 1, six
  days uptime, launchd knows nothing about it — so installing there would hang
  this organ off a leg nobody restarts. Do NOT install on Mini/M5.

  superscar #7 (KeepAlive misconfig): this is a StartInterval PROBE, not a
  daemon — KeepAlive=false, no `nohup ... &`, nothing to restart.

  Kill switch: WA_BOT_THROUGHPUT_SENTINEL_ENABLED=false (honoured in the
  wrapper, which writes its own status=disabled heartbeat before exiting).

  Install:
    cp infra/launchagents/com.nuzantara.wa-bot-throughput-sentinel.plist \
       ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    chmod 444 ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.nuzantara.wa-bot-throughput-sentinel.plist
    launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) \
       ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.nuzantara.wa-bot-throughput-sentinel.plist

  Proof-of-armed is NOT a green exit code and NOT the presence of this file —
  both are the evidence class that let the outage run for 24 days. It is the
  heartbeat sidecar ~/.organism/last_seen/pro.wa_bot_throughput_sentinel.json
  read TWICE at least one interval apart and seen to ADVANCE, plus a negative
  control against a history-free database confirming it reports
  wrong-database rather than dead-channel.

  Plist permissions hardened to 0444 per cicatrix P0-3 — by the chmod in the
  install steps above, which is where it has to live: git cannot carry 0444
  (this blob is 100644, like every other plist here), so before that line
  existed this sentence asserted a property nothing performed.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.nuzantara.wa-bot-throughput-sentinel</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>/Users/nuzantara/nuzantara/scripts/wa_bot_throughput_sentinel_run.sh</string>
    </array>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>HOME</key>
        <string>/Users/nuzantara</string>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin</string>
        <key>WA_BOT_THROUGHPUT_SENTINEL_ENABLED</key>
        <string>true</string>
    </dict>

    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>900</integer>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <key>KeepAlive</key>
    <false/>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/Users/nuzantara/logs/wa-bot-throughput-sentinel.out.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/Users/nuzantara/logs/wa-bot-throughput-sentinel.err.log</string>

    <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
    <integer>60</integer>
</dict>
</plist>
